# trufflehog per-finding allowlist. Each line is one suppressed finding.
#
# Format: <DetectorName>:<full-commit-sha>:<file>:<line> # reason
#
# To add a new entry:
#   1. Run `nix run .#scan`. The wrapper prints each finding's fingerprint
#      (`[DetectorName] file:line (commit)`).
#   2. Append the fingerprint in the format above with a `# reason` comment
#      explaining why it's a false positive. Without a comment, the entry
#      will not pass review.
#
# Empty by default: `--only-verified` is already passed to trufflehog, so
# unverified pattern matches don't appear. Any finding that DOES appear has
# been validated against a live API and is by definition a real secret —
# rotate it, don't whitelist it. The only reason to ever add to this file
# is a test/expired key that trufflehog still considers valid (rare).
